NAME
    tls-nss-sync - reconcile approved m system CAs into a Linux browser NSS database

SYNOPSIS
    tls-nss-sync <effective-browser-home>

DESCRIPTION
    Project the additional public CAs authorized by tls-ca into the NSS
    Shared DB selected for the supplied browser HOME on Linux.

    Existing HOME/.pki/nssdb takes precedence; otherwise use
    HOME/.local/share/pki/nssdb (Chromium M146 onward). Browser profile
    directories and unrelated NSS trust entries are not shared or modified.

    An ownership manifest under HOME/.m/tls-nss-owned records only entries
    managed by this command; a per-HOME Linux flock serializes simultaneous
    projections. Fingerprint-derived nicknames prevent ambiguity. Entries
    outside the ownership manifest cannot be silently taken over.
    Database entry content and SSL CA trust are checked during reconciliation,
    including on subsequent launches, and conflicting entries cause failure.

    If neither approved CAs nor a prior ownership manifest exists, the command
    succeeds without creating an NSS database or requiring NSS tools.

    Removing a CA through tls-ca causes its managed NSS projection to be
    removed at the next synchronization. Already running Chromium/Electron
    processes may retain their previously loaded trust until restart.
    The operating system's independently trusted CAs remain unaffected.

    This is a Linux-specific projection. Non-Linux browser trust backends
    are not silently represented as NSS. The ordinary browser launch requests
    this operation through launcher_nss in pkg-launch.lib.sh.

DEPENDENCIES
    The m core and osarch shell libraries are required to detect the host
    platform independently in this command process.

    For nonempty projection work, certutil from NSS, OpenSSL and Linux flock
    are required. The browser HOME must be a real writable directory.
    Existing NSS DBs with unsupported/password-protected configurations may
    require separate administrator handling; verification is never bypassed.

ENVIRONMENT
    Requires a nonempty m_ROOT inherited from an initialized m environment.
    From an uninitialized host shell, invoke m tls-nss-sync [arguments].


EXIT STATUS
    0     The owned NSS projection is reconciled or no work is necessary.
    2-28  Specific validation, dependency, locking, NSS or filesystem
          failure, diagnosed on stderr with tls-nss-sync.<branch> identity.
    29    Unable to load the m shell runtime.
    30    Unable to load the host-platform shell library.

